From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Julian Vetter <julian.vetter@vates.tech>
Date: Mon, 27 Jul 2026 17:06:50 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] xenopsd/xc: set CDF_TRAP_UNMAPPED_ACCESSES for ARM domains

Xenctrl.domain_create's flags list never included
CDF_TRAP_UNMAPPED_ACCESSES for ARM domains, even though the type
mirror already listed the constructor (see the earlier "mirror
CDF_TRAP_UNMAPPED_ACCESSES from Xenctrl" sync). That was a
compile-time-only fix, the flag itself was never actually set.

Without it, Xen traps guest accesses to unmapped addresses instead of
letting the guest handle them directly. During testing that trap fired
very early in the ARM64 kernel's own head.S (before VBAR_EL1 is
installed), and the resulting injected exception lands at vector offset
0x200, which is itself unmapped -> guest double-faults into an infinite
loop with zero console output.

libxl already sets this flag unconditionally for ARM
(libxl__arch_domain_prepare_config() always includes it in
config->flags), which is why `xl create` with the exact same
kernel/ramdisk/memory boots fine while the identical domain built via
xenopsd never got past its own early boot code. Confirmed by comparing
the actual xen_domctl_createdomain contents both toolstacks send to
xc_domain_create() for the same VM config: xenopsd sent flags=0x3
(CDF_HVM|CDF_HAP), libxl sent flags=0x103 (adding
CDF_TRAP_UNMAPPED_ACCESSES, bit 8).

Signed-off-by: Julian Vetter <julian.vetter@vates.tech>

diff --git a/ocaml/xenopsd/xc/domain.ml b/ocaml/xenopsd/xc/domain.ml
index dde5f78da01c..31b13cde7932 100644
--- a/ocaml/xenopsd/xc/domain.ml
+++ b/ocaml/xenopsd/xc/domain.ml
@@ -415,6 +415,13 @@ let make ~xc ~xs vm_info vcpus domain_config uuid final_uuid no_sharept
         ""
     ) ;
 
+  let is_arm =
+    match (domain_config : arch_domainconfig) with
+    | ARM _ ->
+        true
+    | X86 _ ->
+        false
+  in
   let config =
     {
       ssidref= vm_info.ssidref
@@ -426,6 +433,7 @@ let make ~xc ~xs vm_info vcpus domain_config uuid final_uuid no_sharept
         ; (iommu, CDF_IOMMU)
         ; (nested_virt, CDF_NESTED_VIRT)
         ; (vpmu, CDF_VPMU)
+        ; (is_arm, CDF_TRAP_UNMAPPED_ACCESSES)
         ]
         |> List.filter_map (fun (cond, flag) ->
             if cond then
